The jump from Basic to Pro is the one that matters most: four times the RAM for roughly double the price, which is where most single-app workloads stop swapping. Team only pays off if you're running several services or a database alongside the app — otherwise you're buying headroom you won't touch.

Short answer: Android is more flexible to develop for; iOS is more constrained but usually more profitable to ship for.

:::intelligent-ui{v="1"}
